---
description: Ask the user before acting on unclear requirements or intended behavior.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Clarify uncertainty

- If anything about the user's request or intended behavior is unclear, ask first.
  Do not implement an assumption in place of clarification.
- Clarify API contracts, including return values, output, and failure behavior,
  before changing implementations or callers that depend on those decisions.
- Keep dependent work paused until the user answers. Read-only investigation and
  clearly independent, authorized work may continue.
- Apply corrections precisely; do not introduce additional behavior to fill gaps
  in the request without asking.
